{"id": "EUVD-2026-76396", "enisaUuid": "83da8ed3-ac1f-3276-a62d-185a099ea773", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nocfs2: fix readdir position truncation on 32-bit kernels\n\nIn ocfs2_dir_foreach_blk_el(), the directory cookie position is\nrebuilt with\n\n\tctx->pos = (ctx->pos & ~(sb->s_blocksize - 1)) | offset;\n\n`ctx->pos` is loff_t (signed 64-bit), while `sb->s_blocksize` is\nunsigned long.  On 32-bit kernels unsigned long is 32-bit, so the mask\n\n\t~(sb->s_blocksize - 1)\n\nis computed as a 32-bit unsigned value (e.g. 0xfffff000 for a 4 KiB\nblock size).  In the AND expression with the 64-bit `ctx->pos`, that\nunsigned operand is zero-extended to 64 bits per the usual arithmetic\nconversions, yielding 0x00000000fffff000.  The high 32 bits of\n`ctx->pos` are silently cleared, even though directory size is\nallowed to exceed 4 GiB.\n\nWhen readdir() crosses the 4 GiB boundary on a 32-bit kernel the\nposition is reset back into the first 4 GiB block, making the\nre-validation path re-enumerate already-returned dirents indefinitely.\n\nThis is ocfs2_dir_foreach_blk_el(), the extent-list readdir path taken\nfor all non-inline directories, so a directory large enough to cross\n4 GiB reaches it.\n\nThis is the same class of bug that commit 3dce5bb82c97 (\"exfat: Fix\nbitwise operation having different size\") fixed in exfat, and the\nfix mirrors the equivalent ext4 fix in this series.  Cast the operand\nto loff_t so the mask is 64-bit before the AND:\n\n\tctx->pos = (ctx->pos & ~((loff_t)sb->s_blocksize - 1)) | offset;\n\n64-bit kernels are unaffected.", "datePublished": "2026-09-11T19:43:42", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T08:47:41", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c28dc3407937aa8f225942538cd585c9b28ea65a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/94569154ba49f5f85645d2019c8e206213d8404e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1ae7029823ae4c91664cb32eec7fb8dd5e1a337a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f9dd5cad8d09110ddff2db1fe756aae93c7552ff", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1001fb3b69a11eaa0dc7c7428f6edfa48b88997a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c0c165487a2ea5a37ddcdab4259157b7a527129c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b53e2b271eeb6040c2a4a78230c570dc41cdcfa4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a63308ab426f3a3c7e33b02c150ea59054620261"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-89490", "GHSA-3jg7-r7pg-8654"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "024ba963-2a9a-35b9-a3c3-963fd68fb8d6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ccd979bdbce9fba8412beb3f1de68a9d0171b12c <b53e2b271eeb6040c2a4a78230c570dc41cdcfa4"}, {"id": "0e17de91-5596-3334-bc24-3dec3a0d2e8c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ccd979bdbce9fba8412beb3f1de68a9d0171b12c <94569154ba49f5f85645d2019c8e206213d8404e"}, {"id": "109939b8-8f29-32f3-b1b1-c83da7513362", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ccd979bdbce9fba8412beb3f1de68a9d0171b12c <f9dd5cad8d09110ddff2db1fe756aae93c7552ff"}, {"id": "1d3fa5be-bf5d-3070-b4b7-b0c25be216be", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.109"}, {"id": "207f97d7-afce-3e53-9736-5ec4f099e9fb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ccd979bdbce9fba8412beb3f1de68a9d0171b12c <1ae7029823ae4c91664cb32eec7fb8dd5e1a337a"}, {"id": "26eee3ba-f05e-356a-b7de-69ba1f4c7fdf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.50"}, {"id": "56f1e2df-237d-3a47-b8a5-b5d629a82d42", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.4"}, {"id": "66233ef3-8779-3ecf-a10e-dc6ae2b4969c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.16"}, {"id": "809e8851-5a61-324b-beb9-3639b0279e24", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.15.221"}, {"id": "8a81482a-e91b-340d-b2c7-7a4edb7ff2cf", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "934b2478-cd27-34af-87ca-431b5ac6ccd1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 5.10.270"}, {"id": "9da7bcfc-a729-33ef-a4b8-81bc5fe3550c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ccd979bdbce9fba8412beb3f1de68a9d0171b12c <c28dc3407937aa8f225942538cd585c9b28ea65a"}, {"id": "af234f8b-910e-3fe3-a0e1-7688fcc54e67", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.157"}, {"id": "b04bc4e4-116d-3cf4-9922-47b1049c863a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ccd979bdbce9fba8412beb3f1de68a9d0171b12c <c0c165487a2ea5a37ddcdab4259157b7a527129c"}, {"id": "c9a43b52-fe1e-3a8e-8c5d-cdc9bbef5c4e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ccd979bdbce9fba8412beb3f1de68a9d0171b12c <1001fb3b69a11eaa0dc7c7428f6edfa48b88997a"}, {"id": "cc002891-a81f-3e09-991e-59e4d0db7ce3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.1.188"}, {"id": "db3c30f6-45b7-3df3-be94-df1f7801f0ee", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "e2bbc226-5233-38a6-9fa5-d4df1fd1d420", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ccd979bdbce9fba8412beb3f1de68a9d0171b12c <a63308ab426f3a3c7e33b02c150ea59054620261"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "c05b7e3d-5c0f-3cd7-9ac3-b809ee82e24a", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}